menu "Antenna A/B Test Configuration"

    config AB_WIFI_SSID
        string "Reference AP SSID"
        default "myssid"
        help
            SSID of the access point used as the reference signal source.
            Both antenna runs must target the same AP, on the same channel,
            from the same physical position, or the comparison is meaningless.

    config AB_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Reference AP password"
        default "mypassword"
        help
            WPA2 passphrase for the reference AP. Leave empty for an open AP.

    config AB_WIFI_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Association timeout (ms)"
        range 2000 60000
        default 15000
        help
            How long to wait for association + DHCP before declaring the
            connect attempt failed. A failed connect is itself a result worth
            recording -- the run is stored with connect_ok = false.

    config AB_RSSI_SAMPLES
        int "RSSI samples per run"
        range 10 2000
        default 300
        help
            Number of RSSI readings taken per measurement run. At the default
            200 ms interval, 300 samples is a 60 second run. More samples
            narrow the confidence interval on the mean; fewer get you through
            a demo faster.

    config AB_RSSI_INTERVAL_MS
        int "RSSI sample interval (ms)"
        range 50 5000
        default 200
        help
            Delay between RSSI readings. The ESP32-S3 refreshes the cached
            RSSI on each received beacon, so sampling faster than the AP's
            beacon interval (typically 100 ms) just duplicates readings.

    config AB_PING_COUNT
        int "ICMP echo requests per run"
        range 0 500
        default 50
        help
            RSSI is a receive-side metric only. The ping loss/RTT figures give
            you a round-trip view, which is where a bad transmit path shows up.
            Set to 0 to skip the ping stage.

    config AB_PING_INTERVAL_MS
        int "ICMP echo interval (ms)"
        range 50 5000
        default 200

    config AB_PING_TARGET
        string "ICMP echo target (blank = default gateway)"
        default ""
        help
            Hostname or dotted-quad to ping. Leave blank to ping the DHCP
            default gateway, which keeps the test on the local RF link instead
            of measuring your internet uplink.

    config AB_SCAN_MAX_AP
        int "Maximum APs recorded per scan"
        range 8 128
        default 48
        help
            Upper bound on the AP census. The number of distinct BSSIDs a scan
            can hear is a useful antenna-sensitivity proxy that does not depend
            on any single access point.

endmenu
